{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
	<p><code>render</code> turns a template into a string. Pass the template's name and the variables it should see.</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
const html = await kiln.render("pages/post", {
	route: { path: "/blog/hello/" },
	post,
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<ul>
		<li><code>render</code> always returns a promise, but only waits when a template calls something async.</li>
		<li>If anything goes wrong, the promise rejects and no partial output is returned. See <a href="/docs/api/errors/">Errors and checks</a>.</li>
		<li>Generate <a href="/docs/api/types/">TypeScript types</a> to have your editor check template names and data.</li>
		<li>To send the page while it renders, use <a href="/docs/api/streaming/"><code>renderStream</code></a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Render options</h2>

	<p>The third argument sets options for one render:</p>

	<table>
		<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td><code>state</code></td><td>Data for this request, passed to functions made with <code>withRender</code>. See <a href="/docs/api/extending/#request-data">Request data</a></td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>globals</code></td><td>Globals for this render, layered over the environment's. See <a href="#globals-for-one-render">Globals for one render</a></td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>locale</code></td><td>Overrides the environment's locale</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>timeZone</code></td><td>Overrides the environment's time zone</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>signal</code></td><td>An <code>AbortSignal</code>. Kiln stops the render as soon as it is aborted, even while it waits for your code</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>islands</code></td><td>Defers <a href="/docs/tags/island/"><code>island</code></a> tags with <code>deferIslands()</code>, or streams them with <code>streamIslands()</code> and <code>renderStream</code>. Without it, islands render in place</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
const html = await kiln.render("pages/home", context, {
	locale: "fr-FR",
	timeZone: "Europe/Paris",
	signal: request.signal,
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<h3>Globals for one render</h3>

	<p><code>globals</code> sets variables that every template in the render can read, as <a href="/docs/api/extending/#globals">globals</a> do: the page, its layouts, included templates, components, macros and islands. Use it for a value that is the same for the whole render but changes between renders, such as the locale of the content.</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
const kiln = createKiln({
	loader,
	globals: { site: { name: "Acme" }, contentLocale: "en" },
});

const html = await kiln.render("pages/home", context, {
	globals: { contentLocale: "fr" },
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<ul>
		<li>A render's globals win over the environment's globals of the same name. The environment's other globals stay available.</li>
		<li><code>check</code>, <code>analyze</code>, <a href="/docs/api/types/">generated types</a>, <a href="/docs/tags/export/">exports</a> and your editor only know the environment's globals. Give each per-render global a default there, as <code>contentLocale</code> has above. Otherwise they treat it as render data, and exports can't read it.</li>
		<li>Templates can't assign to them, as with any global.</li>
		<li><a href="/docs/tags/cache/"><code>cache</code></a> keys don't include them. Add any that change a cached section's output to its key.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Rendering one block</h2>

	<p><code>renderBlock</code> renders a single block of a template. Use it to send a fragment of a page, for example in reply to an htmx or <code>fetch</code> request.</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
const results = await kiln.renderBlock("pages/search", "results", { query });
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<ul>
		<li>Kiln picks the block the full page would use, so a page's version wins over its layout's.</li>
		<li>Top-level <code>set</code> tags in the page still run, so data the page loads is available.</li>
		<li>The block doesn't see variables the layout creates around it, such as a <code>for</code> loop's variable.</li>
		<li>Asking for a block that doesn't exist is an error.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Caching</h2>

	<p>Kiln compiles each template the first time it is used, then keeps the compiled version. The loader is called once per template name. If loading or compiling fails, Kiln tries again on the next render.</p>

	<p>Kiln also remembers the last thousand or so names the loader didn't find, so a missing template isn't asked for on every render.</p>

	<p>When a template changes or is added, for example after an edit in your CMS, call <code>invalidate</code>:</p>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
kiln.invalidate("pages/home"); // one template
kiln.invalidate(); // all templates
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}
{% endblock %}
